    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0259" n="171" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg171"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Patenôtre.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 26th of
                    January last, I have the honor to inform you that in view of the announcement
                    conveyed by your note and the previous one of Mr. Desprez, of the assumption by
                    France of a protectorate over African territory heretofore and for many years
                    recognized as belonging to the Republic of Liberia, an instruction on the
                    subject has been sent to the American minister at Paris.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
